NAME
    mkdir - create directories

SYNOPSIS
    mkdir [-pv] DIRECTORY...

DESCRIPTION
    Creates each named DIRECTORY. The parent must already exist and the name
    must be free, unless -p is given.

    -p  Create missing parent directories, and succeed when the directory
        already exists.
    -v  Print a line for each directory created.

    With -p a refusal names the component that caused it rather than the leaf
    that followed, so a mistyped volume reports the mistyped component. That
    needs the filesystem-read capability to tell an ancestor that already
    exists from one that cannot be created, because both refuse alike: /vol
    sits above every writable mount and is no more creatable than a volume
    that does not exist.

    Requires filesystem-mutate to create, and filesystem-read for -p, so it
    works on a writable volume such as /vol/root and is refused on the
    read-only root.

    Every operand is attempted; a failure is reported and the remaining
    operands still run.
